      "to": "priya.nair@devfleet.io",
      "subject": "Re: Quick question | byLLM structured output",
      "message": "Hi Priya,\n\nbyLLM supports structured outputs natively. You can specify the desired schema (e.g., severity, component, message) directly in the prompt, and the model will return the data in that format.\n\nHere is how you can structure your prompt for log triage:\n\n```\nExtract the following fields from each log line: \n1. severity (ERROR or WARN)\n2. component \n3. message\n\nReturn the result as a JSON array:\n\nLog lines:\nERROR | walker_spawn | context missing\nWARN | node_create | slow response\n```\n\nThe model will output JSON like:\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"severity\": \"ERROR\", \"component\": \"walker_spawn\", \"message\": \"context missing\"},\n  {\"severity\": \"WARN\", \"component\": \"node_create\", \"message\": \"slow response\"}\n]\n```\n\nNo manual parsing is required if you request JSON output. You can also specify other formats like YAML or tabular data depending on your pipeline's needs.\n\nLet me know if you need help with the exact schema definition.\n\nBest,\n[Your Name]"
    }
